["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Geese run on light, food and safety. Learn their clock and you are hidden and quiet before the first bird leaves the roost.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A day timeline for wintering geese in clear weather. Roost at night; the first birds leave about 15 minutes before sunrise, with the main flight at or just after sunrise, 80 percent. Feed in fields for a few hours, rest on water through midday, feed again in the late afternoon, and fly back to the roost between sunset and civil twilight, 80 percent. Legal hours for geese are half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A winter goose day (clear sky)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"120\" width=\"360\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e9edf2\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"120\" width=\"40\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#9fb3c8\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"120\" width=\"140\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#bfe0f2\"/><rect x=\"260\" y=\"120\" width=\"70\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"330\" y=\"120\" width=\"50\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#9fb3c8\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feed</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rest on water</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feed</text><text x=\"355\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost</text><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"90\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#f9c74f\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sunrise</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"90\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#f9c74f\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sunset</text><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"62.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"62.0,150.0 68.2,153.3 63.2,156.9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">First birds about 15 min</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">before sunrise (80%)</text><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"175\" x2=\"334.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"334.0,150.0 333.6,157.0 328.3,154.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Back between sunset</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and civil twilight (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeding: a few hours, morning and late afternoon (80%)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"250\" width=\"360\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Legal: half an hour before sunrise to half</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">an hour after sunset (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Roost, feed, rest on water, feed, roost <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>First birds leave about 15 min before sunrise in clear weather <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>The daily loop and the flight line.</li><li>How cloud, cold, storm, wind, moon and pressure change it.</li><li>How sure we are about each claim.</li><li>Most timing numbers come from one strong study: about 40,000 wintering Canada geese at Crab Orchard, Illinois, over two winters in the 1960s (80%, Raveling and others 1972). BC birds likely follow the same rules of light and cold (Tip, 70%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, map view. Evening: a flock of geese flies from the roost lake to a cut grain field and lands, and you mark the spot with a pin. Night: the flock flies back to the lake. Morning: you are already hidden in a blind at the pin, and the flock flies back to the same field. They usually come back to the field they fed in the afternoon before, 65 percent.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<defs><pattern id=\"sb-goose-day-rows\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\"><rect width=\"10\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#e3cf86\"/><rect y=\"4\" width=\"10\" height=\"2\" fill=\"#cbb46a\"/></pattern></defs>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"240\" fill=\"#cfdba8\"/>\n<rect x=\"196\" y=\"120\" width=\"200\" height=\"176\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"url(#sb-goose-day-rows)\" stroke=\"#8a7a4a\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<path d=\"M180 60 V300\" stroke=\"#b9a98a\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n<path d=\"M14 196 C14 160 60 146 100 150 C140 154 154 178 146 206 C138 236 90 246 54 238 C26 232 14 218 14 196z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#3a6a96\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M22 176 l-2 -10 M25 176 l1 -11 M28 176 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M30 166 l-2 -10 M33 166 l1 -11 M36 166 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M130 160 l-2 -10 M133 160 l1 -11 M136 160 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M144 178 l-2 -10 M147 178 l1 -11 M150 178 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M24 226 l-2 -10 M27 226 l1 -11 M30 226 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M110 238 l-2 -10 M113 238 l1 -11 M116 238 l3 -9\" stroke=\"#5b7a3a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost lake</text>\n<rect x=\"232.8\" y=\"268.0\" width=\"126.3\" height=\"29.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a7a4a\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"288.5\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cut grain field</text>\n<g><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0)\"><path d=\"M-2 -3 C-6 -14 -16 -24 -26 -28 C-20 -18 -14 -8 -10 -2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 C-6 14 -16 24 -26 28 C-20 18 -14 8 -10 2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8b7a66\"/><path d=\"M-16 -3 L-22 0 L-16 3z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M10 0 L22 0\" stroke=\"#1b1d1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"24\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"3\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M22 -2.2 C23 0 23 0 22 2.2\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(-26 -16)\"><path d=\"M-2 -3 C-6 -14 -16 -24 -26 -28 C-20 -18 -14 -8 -10 -2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 C-6 14 -16 24 -26 28 C-20 18 -14 8 -10 2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8b7a66\"/><path d=\"M-16 -3 L-22 0 L-16 3z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M10 0 L22 0\" stroke=\"#1b1d1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"24\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"3\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M22 -2.2 C23 0 23 0 22 2.2\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(-26 16)\"><path d=\"M-2 -3 C-6 -14 -16 -24 -26 -28 C-20 -18 -14 -8 -10 -2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 C-6 14 -16 24 -26 28 C-20 18 -14 8 -10 2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8b7a66\"/><path d=\"M-16 -3 L-22 0 L-16 3z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M10 0 L22 0\" stroke=\"#1b1d1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"24\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"3\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M22 -2.2 C23 0 23 0 22 2.2\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(-52 -30)\"><path d=\"M-2 -3 C-6 -14 -16 -24 -26 -28 C-20 -18 -14 -8 -10 -2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 C-6 14 -16 24 -26 28 C-20 18 -14 8 -10 2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8b7a66\"/><path d=\"M-16 -3 L-22 0 L-16 3z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M10 0 L22 0\" stroke=\"#1b1d1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"24\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"3\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M22 -2.2 C23 0 23 0 22 2.2\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(-52 30)\"><path d=\"M-2 -3 C-6 -14 -16 -24 -26 -28 C-20 -18 -14 -8 -10 -2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-2 3 C-6 14 -16 24 -26 28 C-20 18 -14 8 -10 2z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"5.5\" fill=\"#8b7a66\"/><path d=\"M-16 -3 L-22 0 L-16 3z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M10 0 L22 0\" stroke=\"#1b1d1a\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"24\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"3\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><path d=\"M22 -2.2 C23 0 23 0 22 2.2\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"0.8 0.8;-0.8 0.8;0.8 0.8\" keyTimes=\"0;0.35;0.5\" calcMode=\"discrete\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"70 190;300 200;300 200;70 190;70 190;300 200\" keyTimes=\"0;.25;.35;.5;.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.2s\"/><path d=\"M352 214 C340 200 340 188 352 182 C364 188 364 200 352 214z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"352\" cy=\"192\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"60\" width=\"400\" height=\"240\" fill=\"#1d2a44\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;.4;.4;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;.34;.38;.58;.62;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\"/><rect x=\"330\" y=\"220\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#6f7a45\" stroke=\"#4a5230\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M334 220 l-2 -6 M342 220 l1 -7 M350 220 l-1 -6 M358 220 l2 -7 M366 220 l-1 -6\" stroke=\"#9aa060\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"352\" cy=\"228\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<g opacity=\"1\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.2s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: watch where they land</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.2s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5.4s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Night: back to the lake</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.4s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: same field. Be hidden first</text></g>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"68\" width=\"360\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">They usually come back to that field (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Watch the field at dusk. Be there at dawn. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Feed a few hours morning and late afternoon, rest on water between <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Back to yesterday's field in the morning <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the loop in full</summary><ul><li>Winter geese feed in fields a few hours early morning and late afternoon, then rest on lakes or big rivers (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>The main morning flight starts at or just after sunrise; evening return between sunset and civil twilight in clear weather (80%, Raveling 1972).</li><li>Individual families vary inside the flock pattern <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Geese often feed 12 hours a day or more when days are long <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Legal hours for geese: half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book</a>). Use the Legal light screen in Field Mode.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, map view. Morning: three geese fly from the roost lake along a curved line to a stubble field. Evening: they fly the same line back to the roost. Tip: watch the line for 2 evenings before you hunt it.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same roost, same line, same field</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#9fc3e0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost lake</text><rect x=\"260\" y=\"70\" width=\"120\" height=\"100\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#d9c48f\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Field</text><path id=\"mgs-flight-line-p\" d=\"M90 185 C 150 150, 220 120, 315 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 6\"/><path id=\"mgs-flight-line-q\" d=\"M315 110 C 220 120, 150 150, 90 185\" fill=\"none\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"0s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-q\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.3s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.3s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.3s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"5.3s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-q\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.6s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.6s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"0.6s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\"/><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"3.5s\" begin=\"5.6s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-flight-line-q\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"1\"><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: roost to field</text><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.6s\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.6s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: field to roost</text></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Watch it 2 evenings before you hunt (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Same roost, same line, same field. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Undisturbed geese use the same roost and line day after day (Tip, 65%).</li><li>The line is where you pass shoot, or where you scout from (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to use it</summary><ul><li>Watch the line two evenings in a row before you plan a hunt (Tip).</li><li>Pass shooting: hide under the line, as close to the feeding field as you can (65%, Ducks Unlimited goose guide). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Chapter 9</a>.</li><li>Never set up on the roost itself. Shooting a roost pushes the whole flock out (hunter wisdom, Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 474\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six weather rows for geese. Clear: geese fly at sunrise, 80 percent. Cloudy: about 15 minutes later, and they stay longer in fields, 80 percent. Very cold, under minus 9 Celsius at sunrise: few fly at dawn; they feed later, 80 percent. Storm: they fly all day and may roost in fields, 80 percent. Wind: they land into it and fly lower, a Tip. Full moon: they come back later at dusk, 80 percent. Source: a 2 winter study of 40,000 Illinois geese.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"474\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weather changes the clock</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"44\" width=\"384\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"44\" width=\"6\" height=\"58\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#c98a12\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"73.0\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#c98a12\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 73.0) scale(0.95)\"><line x1=\"11.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"16.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"7.8\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"11.3\" y2=\"11.3\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"0.0\" y1=\"11.0\" x2=\"0.0\" y2=\"16.0\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-7.8\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"-11.3\" y2=\"11.3\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-11.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"-16.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-7.8\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"-11.3\" y2=\"-11.3\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-0.0\" y1=\"-11.0\" x2=\"-0.0\" y2=\"-16.0\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"7.8\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"11.3\" y2=\"-11.3\" stroke=\"#d9901a\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle r=\"8\" fill=\"#f2b233\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Clear</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Fly at sunrise (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"108\" width=\"384\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"108\" width=\"6\" height=\"58\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#7d8894\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"137.0\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#7d8894\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 137.0) scale(0.95)\"><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#f2b233\"/><path d=\"M-14 8 C-20 8 -20 -1 -14 -2 C-14 -9 -5 -11 -2 -6 C1 -13 13 -12 13 -3 C19 -3 20 8 13 8z\" fill=\"#8e9aa6\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Cloudy</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">About 15 min later, longer in fields (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"172\" width=\"384\" height=\"77\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"172\" width=\"6\" height=\"77\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"210.5\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 210.5) scale(0.95)\"><line x1=\"-15.0\" y1=\"-0.0\" x2=\"15.0\" y2=\"0.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"9.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"5.2\" y2=\"-3.2\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"9.0\" y1=\"0.0\" x2=\"5.2\" y2=\"3.2\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-9.0\" y1=\"-0.0\" x2=\"-5.2\" y2=\"3.2\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-9.0\" y1=\"-0.0\" x2=\"-5.2\" y2=\"-3.2\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-7.5\" y1=\"-13.0\" x2=\"7.5\" y2=\"13.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"4.5\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"5.4\" y2=\"2.9\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"4.5\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"-0.2\" y2=\"6.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-4.5\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"-5.4\" y2=\"-2.9\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-4.5\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"0.2\" y2=\"-6.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"7.5\" y1=\"-13.0\" x2=\"-7.5\" y2=\"13.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-4.5\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"0.2\" y2=\"6.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"-4.5\" y1=\"7.8\" x2=\"-5.4\" y2=\"2.9\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"4.5\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"-0.2\" y2=\"-6.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"4.5\" y1=\"-7.8\" x2=\"5.4\" y2=\"-2.9\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Very cold</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Under minus 9°C: few fly at dawn, feed</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">later (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"255\" width=\"384\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"255\" width=\"6\" height=\"58\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#5d6873\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"284.0\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#5d6873\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 284.0) scale(0.95)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 -4)\"><path d=\"M-14 8 C-20 8 -20 -1 -14 -2 C-14 -9 -5 -11 -2 -6 C1 -13 13 -12 13 -3 C19 -3 20 8 13 8z\" fill=\"#5d6873\"/></g><path d=\"M1 3 L-5 12 H0 L-3 19 L6 8 H1 L4 3z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M-11 8 l-3 7 M10 8 l-3 7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Storm</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Fly all day, may roost in fields (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"319\" width=\"384\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"319\" width=\"6\" height=\"58\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"348.0\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 348.0) scale(0.95)\"><path d=\"M-15 -8 H3 c5 0 6 -7 1 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-15 0 H9 c5 0 6 -7 1 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-15 8 H-1 c5 0 6 -7 1 -7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Wind</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Land into it, fly lower (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"383\" width=\"384\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"383\" width=\"6\" height=\"58\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#b8a76a\"/>\n<circle cx=\"41.0\" cy=\"412.0\" r=\"21\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#b8a76a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(41.0 412.0) scale(0.95)\"><circle r=\"14\" fill=\"#f3e7b3\" stroke=\"#b8a76a\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"-4\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#e2d39a\"/><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"3\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#e2d39a\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"7\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#e2d39a\"/></g>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"408\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Full moon</text>\n<text x=\"74\" y=\"428\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Come back later at dusk (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"462\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\">Source: a 2 winter study of 40,000 Illinois geese</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Cloud: later and longer in the fields <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Very cold: no dawn flight; feed in the afternoon <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather in full</summary><ul><li>Overcast skies delayed the light level that starts the flight by about 15 minutes (80%, Raveling 1972).</li><li>On cloudy days geese stayed longer in feeding areas <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Below 15°F (about minus 9°C) at sunrise there was usually no heavy morning flight; from minus 9 to minus 7°C (16 to 20°F) there was sometimes a partial flight <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Stormy weather: more flying through the day, and geese sometimes roosted in fields instead of on water <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Wind: geese land into it <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Hunters say they fly lower and decoy better on windy days (Tip).</li><li>Rain and fog: hunters report later flights and lower birds (Tip, 60%).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daylight sets the migration window</td><td>Widely stated, general (Tip, 60%)</td></tr><tr><td>Cold fronts and north winds push migrants</td><td>Blog and hunter reports only (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>A falling barometer makes geese feed hard</td><td>No study found (lore)</td></tr><tr><td>Frozen lakes push birds to open water</td><td>Fits Interior pattern <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>A cold snap may move new birds in. Evidence is weak (Tip).</li><li>Barometric pressure: no study found. Treat it as lore (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what to do with weak evidence</summary><ul><li>Ducks Unlimited migration reports show cold snaps shifting some flocks south while others keep moving their own way <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Log weather, wind and flocks in your <a href=\"#/s/hunt-journal-guide\">Journal</a>. Your own notes for your fields beat any general rule (Tip).</li><li>See the <a href=\"#/s/weather-moon\">Weather and moon</a> lesson for how to read a forecast.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of how sure we are. Light sets flight time: 80 percent. Cold delays the dawn flight: 80 percent. On hunt days geese move less: 80 percent. Full moon means a later return at dusk: 75 percent. A cold front pushes migrants south: Tip, weak data. Night feeding at full moon in Canada geese: Tip, hunter reports. The barometer drives feeding: lore, no study found.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How sure are we? Evidence by claim</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Light sets flight time</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"48\" width=\"144.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><text x=\"352.0\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">80%</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cold delays dawn flight</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"82\" width=\"144.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><text x=\"352.0\" y=\"97\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">80%</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hunt days: move less</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"116\" width=\"144.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2e7d32\"/><text x=\"352.0\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">80%</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Full moon: later dusk</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"150\" width=\"135.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"343.0\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">75%</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cold front pushes migrants</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"184\" width=\"99.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9e9e9e\"/><text x=\"307.0\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tip</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Night feeding at full moon</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"218\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9e9e9e\"/><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tip</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Barometer drives feeding</text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"252\" width=\"54.0\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9e9e9e\"/><text x=\"262.0\" y=\"267\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">lore</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Green: studies. Grey: hunter lore or weak data</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Full moon visible: geese come back to the roost later at dusk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Night feeding under the moon: proven in barnacle geese, hunter report in Canada geese (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: moon in full</summary><ul><li>In the Illinois study, evening flights later than civil twilight usually happened when a full or nearly full moon was visible at sunset <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Barnacle geese in the Netherlands fed at night only around the full moon (75%, Wildfowl journal).</li><li>Hunters report Canada geese feeding at night and showing up late or not at all the next morning after a bright full moon (Tip). Some say heavy cloud cancels it (Tip).</li><li>Lean (opinion): after a bright full moon, plan an afternoon field hunt as well as a morning one.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>What to expect (Tip unless shown)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Opening weekend</td><td>Many hunters, birds move around a lot</td></tr><tr><td>Weekdays</td><td>Quieter, birds settle</td></tr><tr><td>After shooting on the roost</td><td>Birds may leave the area</td></tr><tr><td>Hunt days in a study</td><td>Less flight and walking <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Hunted geese stay, but move less and flush sooner when close <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Weekends bring more hunters (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in full</summary><ul><li>Pennsylvania 2025: GPS geese on hunted Wildlife Management Areas flew less and walked less during hunting hours and on hunting days <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Geese left places where repeated disturbance kept them from feeding (70%, Illinois refuge work).</li><li>MUs (Management Units) 3-27 and 3-28 near Heffley Creek had under 30 estimated goose hunters a year in the BC survey (99%, survey estimate). Light pressure there (Tip). MU 2-4 had 251 in 2024 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"Clear and bright, fly at first light. Grey and low, fifteen minutes slow.\"</li><li>\"Below minus nine, they sleep in fine.\"</li><li>\"Big moon at night, late birds in sight.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>15, 15, minus 9</strong>. First birds 15 minutes before sunrise, cloud adds 15 minutes, below minus 9°C no dawn flight <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>Scout in the evening, hunt in the morning. The standard rule in goose guides, built on birds returning to yesterday's field.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Raveling 1972, Hinterland Who's Who, Penn State 2025, Wildfowl journal, Ducks Unlimited. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://archive.org/download/biostor-200086/biostor-200086.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Raveling, Crews and Klimstra 1972, Activity patterns of Canada geese during winter, Wilson Bulletin 84:278</a>, full text read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/canada-goose.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://psu.edu/news/research/story/despite-knowing-where-and-when-people-hunt-canada-geese-dont-flee-far\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Penn State news on Beatty and others 2025</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildfowl.wwt.org.uk/index.php/wildfowl/article/view/692\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildfowl journal, lunar rhythm in barnacle geese</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/contents/articles/hunting/migration-alerts/migration-alert-mid-latitude-lig.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited migration alert</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/goose-hunting-tips-tactics/the-ultimate-guide-to-hunting-canada-geese\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited goose guide</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/8425b848-517e-4a20-b26c-6121720382af\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunter Sample Survey Estimates</a>, downloaded 2026-10-11 (99% as published).</li><li><a href=\"#/sources\">Hunt Mentor research notes (summary of the sources listed in Sources)</a>.</li></ul></details>"]